  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Diamond weight is named for a seed.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "gem",
        "shape": "round",
        "tone": "#e4eef2"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, traders weighed gems against carob seeds.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "street",
        "name": "A gem trader",
        "role": "Long ago",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#7a5a3a",
            "hair": "short",
            "hairColor": "#2e2420",
            "skin": "#c98e6a",
            "expression": "focused",
            "prop": "magnifier"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The word comes from the Greek name for the seed.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Kerátion",
        "sub": "Greek for the carob seed"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "But each gem center had its own carat.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "journey",
        "from": {
          "name": "Florence",
          "x": 0.2,
          "y": 0.7
        },
        "to": {
          "name": "Amsterdam",
          "x": 0.75,
          "y": 0.25
        },
        "icon": "parcel",
        "label": "Two carats"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In Florence it weighed about 197 milligrams, and in Amsterdam about 206.",
      "say": "In Florence it weighed about one hundred ninety-seven milligrams, and in Amsterdam about two hundred six.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "197 and 206",
        "sub": "Milligrams"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1907 a conference in Paris fixed it at 200 milligrams.",
      "say": "In nineteen oh seven a conference in Paris fixed it at two hundred milligrams.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "study",
        "name": "Paris",
        "role": "1907",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#2a2f3d",
            "hair": "slick",
            "hairColor": "#3a2a1e",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "proud",
            "facial": "mustache"
          },
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#3a3a4a",
            "hair": "short",
            "hairColor": "#b9b4ab",
            "skin": "#f3d6bd",
            "expression": "focused",
            "old": true
          },
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#2a3a2f",
            "hair": "side",
            "hairColor": "#4a3326",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "smile"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "That's one fifth of a gram, split into 100 points.",
      "say": "That's one fifth of a gram, split into one hundred points.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "100 points",
        "sub": "In every carat"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "So a half-carat diamond is 50 points.",
      "say": "So a half-carat diamond is fifty points.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "gift",
        "stone": "round",
        "tone": "#e4eef2",
        "to": "Half a carat",
        "date": "50 points"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The karat that measures gold purity is the same word.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "ring",
        "shape": "round",
        "tone": "#e4eef2",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Karat, with a K"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "So every diamond is still weighed in the name of a seed.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "round",
        "tone": "#e4eef2",
        "label": "Named for a seed",
        "light": "#fff2c4"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "The word carat goes back to the Greek name for the carob seed. Every gem center once had its own carat until 1907, when a conference in Paris fixed it at 200 milligrams.",
